      "widgets_values_named": {
        "tags": "English, male voice, R&B, Brian McKnight, Motown, R&B, high notes, emotional, smooth baritone to falsetto, stacked harmonies, piano, warm bass, 74 BPM ballad",
        "lyrics": "[Verse 1]\n\nI been driving with the radio off\n\nTrying not to hear what I already know\n\nYour perfume still lives in the passenger seat\n\nLike it never got the word to go\n\nI can talk that tough all evening\n\nI can act like I don’t break\n\nBut the second that you cross my mind\n\nI’m a man on his knees again\n[Pre-Chorus]\n\nI don’t need a speech\n\nI don’t need a why\n\nI just need you to walk back through that door\n\nBefore I lose my mind\n[Chorus]\n\nLeave the light on for me, baby\n\nI don’t care how late I get\n\nI been too proud for too long\n\nAnd I’m paying for it yet\n\nIf you still want a bad man\n\nI can be that in the dark\n\nBut when the night gets honest\n\nYou still got my heart\n\nLeave the light\n\nLeave the light on\n[Verse 2]\n\nI know I came home empty\n\nHands full of almost and not enough\n\nYou wanted a man who would stay in the room\n\nNot a ghost that you had to love\n\nI can hit every high note for a crowd\n\nMake the whole place say my name\n\nBut the only voice I’m chasing\n\nIs the one that used to stay\n[Pre-Chorus]\n\nI don’t need a speech\n\nI don’t need a why\n\nI just need you to walk back through that door\n\nBefore I lose my mind\n[Chorus]\n\nLeave the light on for me, baby\n\nI don’t care how late I get\n\nI been too proud for too long\n\nAnd I’m paying for it yet\n\nIf you still want a bad man\n\nI can be that in the dark\n\nBut when the night gets honest\n\nYou still got my heart\n\nLeave the light\n\nLeave the light on\n[Bridge]\n\nTell me I’m wrong\n\nTell me I’m late\n\nTell me you changed the locks and changed your name\n\nI’ll still be outside\n\nEngine running\n\nPraying that hallway still knows my face\n[Final Chorus]\n\nLeave the light on for me, baby\n\nI don’t care how late I get\n\nI been too proud for too long\n\nTo pretend I don’t need you yet\n\nIf the morning comes without you\n\nI’ll live with what I done\n\nBut tonight I’m still that man\n\nAsking you to leave the light on",
        "seed": 0,
        "control_after_generate": "fixed",
        "bpm": 120,
        "duration": 120,
        "timesignature": "4",
        "language": "en",
        "keyscale": "E minor",
        "generate_audio_codes": true,
        "cfg_scale": 2,
        "temperature": 0.85,
